e anything that requires Rage or change shapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T07:01:21-07:00","id":1194518,"title":"","content":"In earlier editions, losing the wolf required zero points to spend in Rage and Willpower. Not sure on W20.<br /> <br /> And it means, that they loose the ability to shape change and obviouly to spend rage, but it doesn't hinder them in any other way, iirc.<br /> Their permanent Rage still triggers the Curse, for example.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:06:31-07:00","id":1197156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194416-losing-the-wolf-and-stepping-sideways?p=1194518#post1194518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In earlier editions, losing the wolf required zero points to spend in Rage and Willpower. Not sure on W20.<br /> <br /> And it means, that they loose the ability to shape change and obviouly to spend rage, but it doesn't hinder them in any other way, iirc.<br /> Their permanent Rage still triggers the Curse, for example.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It works the same in W20, once you reach 0 temporary points in both Rage and Willpower you lose the wolf. And indeed, their other abilities remain uninterrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}